<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Russo-Polish War (1654–1667)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1654">1654</a>–<a href="/years/1667">1667</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Russo-Polish War of 1654–1667 was fought between the Tsardom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish–Lithuanian Commonwealth</a>, after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossack-hetmanate">Cossack Hetmanate</a> placed itself under the tsar at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pereiaslav">Pereiaslav</a>. Russia overran much of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Grand Duchy of Lithuania</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/truce-of-andrusovo">Truce of Andrusovo</a> (1667) gave it <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smolensk">Smolensk</a> and left-bank <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kyiv</a>, marking a lasting shift of power in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/russo-polish-war-1654-1667.jpg" alt="Russo-Polish War (1654–1667)" width="320" height="247" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Osada_Liahovich_1660.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
